WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.000
How do we classify triangles?

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.800
One way in which they can be classified is the lengths of their sides.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.480
Let's see how?

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.280
So based on sides, the first kind of triangle is a triangle

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.940
which has all its sides equal to each other.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.040
To show that they are equal.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.480
we put the same mark on each of the sides.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.600
This tells us that all three sides are equal.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:33.140
Such triangles are called equilateral triangles.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.860
Remember, all sides have to be equal.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.440
The word by itself tells you that.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:41.940
Equi is equal.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.180
And lateral is side.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:48.540
The other kind of triangle is a triangle which has two sides equal.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.820
Say these two sides.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.500
Such triangles are called Isosceles triangles.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.800
Any two of the three sides can be equal.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.400
And the third type of triangle is the one in which no two sides are equal.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:07.420
Such triangles are called scalene triangles.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.040
Remember, the length of each side of the scalene

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.660
triangle is different from the other.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:17.760
So this was the classification of triangles based on sides.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.600
The other way in which they can be classified.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.940
is the measure of its angles.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:26.700
Let us review the topic of Angles a bit .

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.520
If an angle is less than 90 degrees it is called acute.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.880
The angle will look something like this.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.900
If it equals 90 degrees then it's called a right angle.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.460
Which will look exactly like this.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:44.980
And if it's greater than 90 degrees, then it's called an obtuse angle.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.100
This is how it will look.

00:01:47.539 --> 00:01:49.429
Here's the good news.

00:01:49.429 --> 00:01:52.760
Triangles are also classified in a similar way.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:58.060
Look at this triangle ,all the angles inside are acute.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.900
Any guesses on what such triangles are called?

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.359
Yes,

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.220
acute triangles.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.240
Now look at this triangle

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.040
This angle here is a right angle.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:15.060
If one angle in a triangle is a right angle. Then it's called a right triangle.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:19.420
It's also referred to as a right-angled triangle.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.540
Remember, just one angle has to be a right angle,

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.660
for the triangle to be a right triangle.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.220
On that note let me ask you a random question.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:33.320
Can we have two right angles in a triangle.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:38.060
Try making one in your notebook, and you will get your answer.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:43.460
The third kind of triangle looks a bit like this. If you observe carefully.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:47.160
You will see that just one angle is obtuse.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:52.140
A triangle in which one angle is obtuse, is called an obtuse angle.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:56.160
This angle in the triangle is greater than 90 degrees

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.160
which makes it obtuse.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:01.820
So this was the basic classification of triangles.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.140
To revisit what we have covered so far

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:08.060
please go through the summary at the end of this video.

